# Allowlist, not a denylist. `outputDirectory` in vercel.json controls what is
# *served*; it does not control what is *uploaded*. The Vercel CLI transmits the
# project source tree to Vercel's build infrastructure on every deploy, so without
# this file `memory/` (project decisions, learnings, event traces), `tasks/`,
# `reports/` (generated reports, present in the working
# tree), `PROJECT_KANBAN*.md`, and `docs/` would all be sent to a third party on
# every `vercel` invocation. Enumerating what to exclude would fail open the first
# time a new directory is added, so deny everything and admit only what the deploy
# needs. Caveat: whether Vercel honours this file on the automatic Git-integration
# path is not established (see PROJECT_SPEC_SITE.md).
*
!site/
!site/**
!vercel.json
